strates the section where we have 25  genes found in this party  a gene expression study that was  published in geo from Crohn's disease  versus healthy control and these are the  top 25 genes and what you can see here  is that these genes are very strongly up  regulated in response to Crohn's disease  this is actually what we were screening  for in the differential expression we  see that they are also strongly up  regulated in ulcerative colitis which is  a related disease so it's not really  surprising they are also to a certain  extent regulated in colorectal at  enormous and all of them are very  strongly down regulated in response to  infliximab  which is one of the frequent drugs used  to treat crohn's disease so there is a  clear interaction between the expression  in in response to the drug and  expression in the in the disease itself  so this is a very nice result that we  can see here we see the same results  also in the top 25 genes that were found  in our analysis for where we screen for  genes that are only or maximally  expressed in Crohn's disease and  minimally expressed elsewhere but now  since we had been screening for genes  that are specific for Crohn's disease if  we add other diseases I as I have added  here these are not all that we tested  it's just an example to illustrate it  but for example here in in these  inflammatory diseases we can see that  the genes found to be top regulated if  you do a differential expression in this  study were also regulated in quite a  number of other inflammatory diseases  whereas in our approach the genes we  found were specific for crohn's disease  they were not regulated in these other  inflammatory diseases either so it  allowed us to screen 14 that are really  specific for the disease of interest and  not involved in other things which makes  them much more interesting in a certain  way or attractive to be  as novel targets for the disease unless  you want to develop a drug that can be  applied to other 